VERDICT
========================================================================================================
  1. THE PUBLISHED NUMBER: OR24's a0 ~ sqrt(Lambda) holds as a SCALING, but its coefficient is
     kappa = 1.30-1.45 (completely positive beta), >= 11 sigma above the measured 0.465 +/- 0.076;
     kappa = 1/2 needs beta = 0.2353, which gives up complete positivity. As a Tully-Fisher
     normaliser it tends to 2 c H_Lambda (Milgrom 1999) at beta -> -inf. Its gamma_1 r term is a constant
     acceleration: lensing-RAR slope 0 vs 0.537 +/- 0.026 measured (L248), 20 sigma.
  2. THE CLASS: a phantom made of GR-COMPLIANT fluctuation energy (waves; every quantum graviton bath) is dead
     on lensing at 11 sigma, convention-free. A phantom made of CONSTRAINT-VIOLATING static scalar noise
     (what CQ gravity uniquely allows) is NOT excluded: under the Einstein-Langevin convention it must lens
     >= 3.8% MORE than it attracts (1.6 sigma today; OR24's own ansatz
     6.2%, 2.6 sigma); a two-component spectrum can null the difference. Pure lapse
     noise and OR24's white-in-time limit rectify to REPULSION.
  3. THE MISSING INPUT, named: CQ gravity does not say which tensor density its noise is unbiased in, and the
     lensing prediction moves at O(1) with that choice. Until it does, the class is open-but-unpriced.
  4. NOTHING HERE DERIVES kappa OR THE AMPLITUDE: the noise must track the phantom (rms ~1135 x the mean
     field at r_M) and D0 is free. A door opened with a price tag and a falsifier, not a closure.

